      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "APA 7th style requires you to list the first author's last name followed by \"et al.\" (and the other required referencing information) after the first mention in the text, except for the first and second publications. Chicago style typically would have you include all the author names after the first citation for in-text references as well.\n\nFor instance, in APA 7th, your first mention would look like this: (Smith et al., 2020). For subsequent references, you would use (Smith et al., 2020, p. 15).\n\nIn Chicago style, your first mention might look like this: Smith, John, et al. \"Title.\" Journal Name, vol. XX, no. XX, 2020, p. 15.\n\nRemember, these are just templates and you'll need to adjust them according to your specific book or article and your use case.",
